                                "sense_id": "289542ae-e7f5-3b56-9a81-3ff7a011646b",
                                "text": "Beautiful peepshows with hand-coloured engravings by Martin Englebrecht, 1684-1756, were produced in Augsburg about 1740. The box, about six inches cube, contained slots to take four cut-out scenes, the front of the box had another cut-out, and the back was painted with a landscape, making six 'curtains' in all."
                            }
